/-!
# Tensor products of the sheaves associated to graded modules on Proj

Let `S` be a commutative ring with a nonnegative grading `𝒮 : ℕ → σ`, and let `M` and `N` be
`ℤ`-graded `S`-modules. The tensor product `M ⊗[S] N` is graded by the additive subgroups
generated by the pure tensors of homogeneous elements whose degrees add up, and there is a
canonical morphism

  `M̃ ⊗_{𝒪} Ñ ⟶ (M ⊗[S] N)~`

of sheaves of modules on `Proj(S)`. It is built by sheafifying the map that sends a pure
tensor of sections to the pointwise tensor of their values, read through the identification
of the localization of a tensor product with the tensor product of the localizations.

On a positive-degree standard open `D₊(f)` the morphism is the expected formula on
fractions: `m/f^p ⊗ n/f^q ↦ (m ⊗ n)/f^{p+q}`; on stalks it is the corresponding formula on
germs.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.tensorGrading_decomposition`: the
  homogeneous pieces of the tensor grading decompose `M ⊗[S] N`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.tensorGrading_gradedSMul`: the tensor
  grading is compatible with the graded scalar action of `S`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.associatedModuleSheafTensorMap`: the
  canonical morphism of sheaves.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.associatedModuleSheafTensorMap_standardOpen`:
  the formula for the morphism on sections over a positive-degree standard open.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.associatedModuleSheafTensorMap_stalk`:
  the formula for the morphism on the stalk at a homogeneous prime of a standard open.

## Implementation notes

The grading of `M ⊗[S] N` is the one already defined for the twisting construction,
`Stacks.GradedModule.tensorGrading`; what is added here is its decomposition and its
compatibility with the graded action, which the associated-sheaf construction needs as
instances. The decomposition is produced by transporting the decompositions of `M` and `N`
through `TensorProduct.directSum` over `ℤ` and collapsing the resulting bigrading along the
sum of the degrees; the collapse is additive and `S`-balanced, and `S`-balancedness is
checked on homogeneous elements, which is where the graded action of `𝒮` is used.

The tensor product of sheaves is the sheafification of the pointwise tensor-product
presheaf, so the morphism out of it is obtained from the sheafification adjunction applied to
a morphism of presheaves of modules. Its value on the image of a pure tensor of honest
sections is therefore the presheaf-level formula, which is what makes the standard-open and
stalk formulas computable.

The compatibility of the morphism with the canonical maps from degree-zero elements into
global sections, which is the remaining assertion of Tag 01MK, is phrased over the
degree-zero global sections map; that map does not exist in this library yet, so that
assertion is not proved here and is absent.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

